..         Terminal handler for the Marinchip PROM/RAM/SIO/RTC board..                                       John Walker   July 1978.                                       David Hunter  May  2014...         This program provides the character-level handling for the serial.         I/O port on the Marinchip PROM/RAM board.  It provides automatic.         baud rate detection on initialisation.  When the routine TRESET.         is called, the user is expected to type a single space.  The.         routine will automatically calculate the ratio of the terminal.         bit rate to the CPU clock, and program the port for the proper.         baud rate.  The method used will accept any baud rate between.         110 and 9600 (continuously variable!!!), and in addition, 19.2KB..         (No speed between 9600 and 19200 is permitted).  Note that this.         is done from the depression of a SINGLE SPACE!  The exercise of.         figuring out how this was done is left to the reader of this code...         This routine can also be configured to bypass the reset baud.         rate sensing.  This is for programs which operate in an.         environment where the port is known to be already properly.         programmed.....         (C)  Copyright 1978   Marinchip Systems..                   All Rights Reserved..         The  information contained herein is confidential, proprietary.         to Marinchip Systems, and considered a trade secret as defined.         in  section 499C of the penal code of the State of California..         Use  of  this  information is granted  only through  a written.         authorisation  by  Marinchip Systems expressly prescribing the.         scope and manner of such use..          idt       "TERM9902"          copy      "../systemdef/sysdef"...         CRU device address of serial I/O port.devadr    equ       000...         TMS9902 Output CRU bit assignments.oblxdr    equ       11                  load transmit data rateoblrdr    equ       12                  load receiver data rateobldir    equ       13                  load interval timer registerobldctrl  equ       14                  load control registerobtstmd   equ       15                  set test modeobrtson   equ       16                  request to send onobbrkon   equ       17                  transmit line breakobrienb   equ       18                  receiver interrupt enableobxienb   equ       19                  transmitter interrupt enableobtimenb  equ       20                  timer interrupt enableobdscenb  equ       21                  data set status change enableobreset   equ       31                  reset device..         TMS9902 Input CRU bit assignments.ibrcverr  equ       9                   receive erroribrper    equ       10                  receive parity erroribrover   equ       11                  receive overrunibrfer    equ       12                  receive framing erroribrfbd    equ       13                  receive full bit detectibrsbd    equ       14                  receive start bit detectibrin     equ       15                  receive inputibrbint   equ       16                  receiver interruptibxbint   equ       17                  transmitter interruptibtimint  equ       18                  timer interrupribdscint  equ       20                  data set change interruptibrbrl    equ       21                  receive buffer loadedibxbre    equ       22                  transmitter buffer register emptyibxsre    equ       23                  transmitter shift register emptyibtimerr  equ       24                  timer error (not serviced in time)ibtimelp  equ       25                  time elapsedibrts     equ       26                  request to sendibdsr     equ       27                  data set readyibcts     equ       28                  clear to sendibdsch    equ       29                  data set status changeibflag    equ       30                  register load control flag setibint     equ       31                  interrupt pending..         TMS9902 Control register bits.crsb1     equ       080                 1 stop bitcrsb1p5   equ       0                   1.5 stop bitscrsb2     equ       040                 2 stop bitscrpenb    equ       020                 parity enablecrpodd    equ       010                 odd parity selectcrclk4m   equ       8                   divide clock by 4 if 1, 3 if 0crlen5    equ       0                   5 bit charactercrlen6    equ       1                   6 bit charactercrlen7    equ       2                   7 bit charactercrlen8    equ       3                   8 bit character...         Configuration equates..         CRU address of serial port.          page..         Reset terminal I/O handler..         BL        TRESET.         <return>                      R0 - R3, R12 destroyed..         This routine performs the automatic baud rate sensing.  Hence,.         the user will have to go through the automatic sense sequence.         every time this is called..treset*   .          li        r12,devadr          load CRU device address          sbo       obreset             reset the 9902          c         *r11,*r11           delay          ldcr      control,8           set serial I/O modes          sbz       obldir              no timer          ldcr      baud96,12           load baud rate          sbz       obxienb             no tx interrupt          sbz       obrienb             no rx interrupt          sbo       obrtson             turn on transmitter (rts)          rt        .                   return to caller..         Data to initialise port.control   byte      crsb1+crlen7+crpenb 1 stop bit, even par,.                                       8 bit character          evenbaud96    data      0034                baud 9600                          ...         Test character available from keyboard..         BL        TRSTAT.         JEQ       <no character available>.         <return>                      R2, R12 destroyed regardless of return.trstat*   li        r12,devadr          load address of SIO port          seto      r2                  set R2 to something else          tb        ibrbrl              is character available ?          jeq       trstat1             yes.  go to return nonzero status          c         r2,r2               no.  set equal status bit          rt        .                   return to caller.trstat1   c         r2,r12              compare unequal values          rt        .                   and return with character status...         Read character from keyboard..         BL        TREADCH.         <return>                      R2 = character (RJZF).                                       R12 destroyed.treadch*  li        r12,devadr          load CRU device address          stcr      r2,8                read in character          srl       r2,8                right justify character          sbz       obrienb             turn off character available flag          rt        .                   return to caller...         Check terminal ready for output character..         BL        TWSTAT.         JEQ       <not ready>.         <return>                      R3, R12 destroyed.twstat*   li        r12,devadr          load CRU device address          seto      r3                  set R3 to something else          tb        ibxbre              transmitter ready for character ?          jeq       twstat1             yes.  go to return nonzero status          c         r3,r3               no.  set equal status bit          rt        .                   return to caller.twstat1   c         r3,r12              compare nonzero values          rt        .                   and return with ready status...         Send character to terminal..         LI        R2,<character>.         BL        TWRITECH.         <return>                      R12 destroyed.twritech* li        r12,devadr          load CRU device address          swpb      r2                  yes.  move character to upper byte          ldcr      r2,8                send character to transmitter          swpb      r2                  put character back in low byte          rt        .                   return to caller..          end       .